-- title:
--   Flat adic Galois representation from a Hecke eigen-piece
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N\ge 1$, $S$ a set of naturals, and $\mathcal{O}'$ a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with finite residue field and with $p$ in its maximal ideal; let $K$ be a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}'$. Let $M$ be a finite free $\mathcal{O}'$-module carrying a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}M$ and a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from the abstract Hecke ring $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell]_{\ell\text{ prime}}$ to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}M$, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathcal{O}'$ from the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q\mid N$, $q\notin S$). Assume: (hES) there is a $2$-dimensional $K$-subspace $W\subseteq K\otimes_{\mathcal{O}'}M$, stable under all base-changed $\rho_M(\sigma)$, on which each base-changed $T_M(X_\ell)$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) acts as the scalar $\chi(T_\ell)$, and such that for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field, the trace on $W$ of $\rho_M(\sigma)$ equals $\chi(T_\ell)$; (hquad) for such $\ell,A,\sigma$ the relation $\rho_M(\sigma)^2-T_M(X_\ell)\rho_M(\sigma)+\ell=0$ holds on $M$; (hunr) for primes $q\nmid N$, $q\ne p$, the inertia subgroups of all valuation subrings over $q$ act trivially; (hcont) $\rho_M$ is adically continuous, i.e. for each $n$ some finite subextension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ has $\rho_M(\sigma)v-v\in\mathfrak{m}^n M$ for all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise; (hFF) for every $k$ there are a commutative ring $H$ with a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over the subring $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}\subseteq\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals with denominator coprime to $p$, finite and flat over it, and a bijection $e$ from the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $H\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (with their convolution product) onto $M/p^kM$ sending products to sums and satisfying $e(\sigma\circ f)=\rho_M(\sigma)\,e(f)$. Then there exists an adic Galois representation over $\mathcal{O}'$ — a rank-two finite free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ with an adically continuous $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$-action $\rho$ — such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for a valuation subring over $\ell$ the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\chi(T_\ell)X+\ell$, the inertia at every prime $q\nmid N$, $q\ne p$ acts trivially, and $\rho$ is flat at $p$: the residue field is finite and for every ideal $I$ with $\mathcal{O}'/I$ finite the level $V/IV$ is, additively and Galois-equivariantly, the set of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of a finite flat commutative cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$.
--
--   This is the flat refinement of the passage from a Hecke eigen-piece in a Galois-and-Hecke module to a two-dimensional $\mathcal{O}'$-adic representation with prescribed Frobenius characteristic polynomials: finite flatness of all levels of the ambient module is propagated to the constructed lattice, using that subquotients of finite flat group schemes over a discrete valuation ring remain finite flat. It is used in [`CuspForm.isFlatAt_of_point_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.isFlatAt_of_point_of_not_dvd) and in [`RibetIrr.irreducible_of_point_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#RibetIrr.irreducible_of_point_of_not_dvd), which supply the local conditions at $p$ needed on the modular side of the Frey curve argument.
